
  <sn><md>### Properties of Soil Inorganic Colloids

**Soil inorganic colloids** are very `small, negatively or positively charged mineral particles`, mainly **clay minerals, Fe/Al oxides, and amorphous aluminosilicates**. They are generally smaller than **2 µm** and have a very large surface area.

![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-emon/QDoc/main/SES3/Soil%20and%20Enviromental%20Chemistry/01.Concept%20of%20Soil%20and%20Enviromental%20Chemistry/assets/soil_inorganic_colloid_thumbnail.jpeg)

</md></sn>
